.TH SESSLINT-OUTCOME 1 "" "SessLint 0.5.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-outcome \- [read\-only] Verify an outcome contract against source/target snapshots.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint outcome [\-\-explain] [\-\-source SOURCE] [\-\-target TARGET] [\-\-as\-of AS_OF] [\-\-source\-observed\-at SOURCE_OBSERVED_AT] [\-\-source\-completeness {complete,partial,unknown,unavailable}] [\-\-source\-origin {target_system,workflow_log,user_file,manual}] [\-\-target\-observed\-at TARGET_OBSERVED_AT] [\-\-target\-completeness {complete,partial,unknown,unavailable}] [\-\-target\-origin {target_system,workflow_log,user_file,manual}] [\-\-session SESSION] [\-\-hash\-keys] [\-\-all\-conditions] [\-\-max\-file\-bytes MAX_FILE_BYTES] [\-f | \-\-format {human,json}] [\-\-json] [\-o | \-\-output FILE] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose] CONTRACT
.SH DESCRIPTION
OutcomeGuard: reconcile work items in a source snapshot with results in a target snapshot, per a declared contract. Offline and read\-only; absence is proven only from a complete target snapshot observed after the deadline.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B CONTRACT
sesslint.outcome\-contract/v1 JSON file
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Validate the contract and print what it checks; read no snapshots
.TP
.B \-\-source SOURCE
Source snapshot (.csv/.json/.jsonl)
.TP
.B \-\-target TARGET
Target snapshot (.csv/.json/.jsonl)
.TP
.B \-\-as\-of AS_OF
Evaluation instant (default: the target observation time; no wall clock)
.TP
.B \-\-source\-observed\-at SOURCE_OBSERVED_AT
When the source snapshot was taken (UTC offset required)
.TP
.B \-\-source\-completeness {complete,partial,unknown,unavailable}
Declared completeness of the source snapshot (default: unknown) Choices: complete, partial, unknown, unavailable.
.TP
.B \-\-source\-origin {target_system,workflow_log,user_file,manual}
Where the source snapshot came from (default: user_file) Choices: target_system, workflow_log, user_file, manual.
.TP
.B \-\-target\-observed\-at TARGET_OBSERVED_AT
When the target snapshot was taken (UTC offset required)
.TP
.B \-\-target\-completeness {complete,partial,unknown,unavailable}
Declared completeness of the target snapshot (default: unknown) Choices: complete, partial, unknown, unavailable.
.TP
.B \-\-target\-origin {target_system,workflow_log,user_file,manual}
Where the target snapshot came from (default: user_file) Choices: target_system, workflow_log, user_file, manual.
.TP
.B \-\-session SESSION
Session file you link to this run (user\-asserted); checked, never modified
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-keys
Show keys as truncated SHA\-256 pseudonyms (pseudonymous, not anonymous)
.TP
.B \-\-all\-conditions
List every condition result for passing items too (default: problems only)
.TP
.B \-\-max\-file\-bytes MAX_FILE_BYTES
Default: 104857600.
.TP
.B \-f {human,json}, \-\-format {human,json}
Output format (default: human) Choices: human, json.
.TP
.B \-\-json
.TP
.B \-o FILE, \-\-output FILE
Write the report to FILE instead of stdout (existing report files are overwritten atomically)
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
a clean session exits 0
(also verification passed / dry-run plan generated)
.TP
.B 1
a session with findings exits 1
(also verification failed / repair refused)
.TP
.B 2
an internal tool error exits 2
(also usage error / invalid flags / I/O failure)
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
(docs/SPEC.md, docs/codes/, docs/recipes/, docs/adr/, docs/THREAT_MODEL.md),
or the project site.
.fi

